        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Wadleigh, Barbara Kopple, Cathy Caplan, Thomas Haneke, Lawrence Silk\n- Films: Woodstock, American Dream\n- Events: Woodstock Festival\n- Places: Bethel, New York, Akron, Ohio\n\nFacts:\n- The Woodstock Festival took place in August 1969 near Bethel, New York.\n- Woodstock is a 1970 documentary film about the watershed counterculture Woodstock Festival.\n- Michael Wadleigh was born on September 24, 1942, in Akron, Ohio.\n- Michael Wadleigh, also known as Michael Wadley, is an American film director and cinematographer.\n- Michael Wadleigh is renowned for his documentary film Woodstock about the 1969 Woodstock Festival.\n- American Dream is a 1990 cinéma vérité documentary film.\n- Barbara Kopple directed American Dream.\n- Cathy Caplan, Thomas Haneke, and Lawrence Silk co-directed American Dream.",
